  ================================================================
  Physical robot based on actual measurements and photos.

  FRAME CONVENTION  (ROS REP-103)
    X = forward   Y = left   Z = up
    base_link origin = center of drive wheel axle, at wheel-axle height
    base_footprint  = directly below base_link on the ground

  TO CHANGE CAMERA HEIGHT:
    Edit only:  zed_mount_z_above_base_plate  (and/or zed_mount_x_from_base_link)
    Everything else (rods, base holder) stays fixed.

  TO CHANGE ANY OTHER DIMENSION:
    Edit the corresponding property at the top of this file.

  COORDINATE NOTES
    All joint origins are expressed relative to parent link origin.
    base_plate_top_z_from_axle  = ply_t + ground_clearance - wheel_radius
      = 0.005 + 0.03 - 0.05 = -0.015 m  (base plate top is 1.5 cm BELOW axle)
  ================================================================
-->
